      text: "The final weeks of the semester arrived faster than anyone expected.\n\nWhat had once seemed distant was suddenly standing right in front of them.\n\nGraduation.\n\nFor months, students had talked about it.\n\nPlanned for it.\n\nDreamed about it.\n\nNow it was finally here.\n\nThe campus felt different.\n\nConversations carried a sense of urgency.\n\nPhotographs were taken everywhere.\n\nGroups of friends gathered beneath trees and outside lecture halls, trying to preserve memories before everyone went their separate ways.\n\nSome students were excited.\n\nOthers were nervous.\n\nMany were both.\n\nFor Brian, graduation represented something more than the end of university.\n\nIt represented the beginning of real life.\n\nThe safety of classrooms would soon disappear.\n\nAssignments would be replaced by responsibilities.\n\nDreams would finally meet reality.\n\nOne afternoon, after submitting one of his final projects, Brian walked slowly across the campus.\n\nStudents surrounded him.\n\nLaughter filled the air.\n\nYet he couldn't shake the feeling that an important chapter of his life was closing.\n\nHe found Diana sitting beneath their usual tree.\n\nShe smiled when she saw him.\n\n\"Done?\"\n\n\"Finally.\"\n\n\"How does it feel?\"\n\nBrian sat beside her.\n\n\"Strange.\"\n\nShe laughed.\n\n\"You? Strange?\"\n\n\"Yes.\"\n\n\"I thought you'd be celebrating.\"\n\n\"I am.\"\n\n\"Then why do you look worried?\"\n\nBrian looked toward the library building.\n\n\"Because now everything becomes real.\"\n\nDiana nodded.\n\nShe understood.\n\nGraduation sounded exciting until it actually arrived.\n\nThen the questions began.\n\nWhat comes next?\n\nWhat if things don't work out?\n\nWhat if the future doesn't look the way we imagined?\n\nFor a few moments they sat quietly.\n\nWatching students move around campus.\n\nWatching a chapter of life slowly come to an end.\n\n\"What are your plans?\" Diana asked.\n\nBrian smiled.\n\n\"The same as always.\"\n\n\"Become a billionaire?\"\n\n\"That would be nice.\"\n\nShe laughed.\n\n\"No, seriously.\"\n\n\"I want to start building something.\"\n\n\"A business?\"\n\n\"Yes.\"\n\n\"Immediately?\"\n\n\"As soon as possible.\"\n\nDiana shook her head.\n\n\"You never stop.\"\n\nBrian smiled.\n\nNeither of them knew how much that determination would shape the years ahead.\n\nA few days later, graduation finally arrived.\n\nFamilies filled the university grounds.\n\nParents walked proudly beside their children.\n\nCameras flashed constantly.\n\nGraduates posed for photographs with friends and lecturers.\n\nThe atmosphere was filled with excitement and emotion.\n\nBrian's parents had traveled to attend the ceremony.\n\nSeeing the pride in their eyes made every sacrifice worthwhile.\n\nYears of studying.\n\nLate nights.\n\nFinancial struggles.\n\nDifficult exams.\n\nEverything had led to this moment.\n\nWhen his name was called, Brian walked across the stage and received his certificate.\n\nThe applause lasted only seconds.\n\nYet the moment would stay with him forever.\n\nAfter the ceremony, students gathered everywhere for photographs.\n\nPromises filled the air.\n\n\"We'll stay in touch.\"\n\n\"We should meet again.\"\n\n\"Don't disappear.\"\n\nEveryone said the same things.\n\nSome meant them.\n\nOthers didn't.\n\nLife had a way of pulling people apart.\n\nLater that afternoon, Brian found Diana standing with several friends.\n\nFor a moment, neither spoke.\n\nThe reality of the day finally settling in.\n\n\"So this is it,\" Diana said.\n\nBrian nodded.\n\n\"I guess it is.\"\n\nFor a brief moment, the noise around them seemed to fade.\n\nThe years of lectures.\n\nRehearsals.\n\nConversations.\n\nFriendships.\n\nEverything suddenly felt like a memory.\n\n\"Don't forget us when you're rich,\" Diana joked.\n\nBrian laughed.\n\n\"I'm not rich yet.\"\n\n\"Yet.\"\n\nThe confidence in her voice made him smile.\n\nThey exchanged numbers again, even though they already had them.\n\nAlmost as if they wanted reassurance that the connection would continue.\n\nThen they hugged goodbye.\n\nA simple gesture.\n\nYet it carried more meaning than either of them expected.\n\nAs Brian walked away, he turned once and saw Diana waving.\n\nHe waved back.\n\nNeither knew when they would see each other again.\n\nThe following months were difficult.\n\nUniversity life disappeared overnight.\n\nThe familiar routines were gone.\n\nThe structure that had guided life for years vanished.\n\nFor Brian, the real world arrived quickly.\n\nHe moved into a small office space with two friends and began working on business ideas.\n\nMost of them failed.\n\nA few survived.\n\nMoney was scarce.\n\nSome months were better than others.\n\nThere were days when doubt crept in.\n\nDays when employment seemed like the easier option.\n\nBut Brian refused to give up.\n\nHe had always believed in building something of his own.\n\nNow he was finally trying.\n\nMeanwhile, Diana returned home and continued pursuing her own goals.\n\nLife became busy.\n\nDifferent.\n\nDemanding.\n\nThe distance between them grew naturally.\n\nNot because either wanted it.\n\nSimply because adulthood had arrived.\n\nTheir conversations became less frequent.\n\nA text message every few weeks.\n\nAn occasional phone call.\n\nBirthday wishes.\n\nHoliday greetings.\n\nNothing more.\n\nMonths turned into years.\n\nThe friendship remained.\n\nBut it existed quietly in the background.\n\nSometimes weeks passed without communication.\n\nThen one of them would suddenly reach out.\n\n\"How have you been?\"\n\nThe conversation would continue for a while before life pulled them away again.\n\nDuring those years, both of them changed.\n\nBrian learned what it meant to struggle.\n\nHe learned that ambition alone was not enough.\n\nSuccess demanded patience.\n\nPersistence.\n\nSacrifice.\n\nDiana learned her own lessons.\n\nAbout work.\n\nResponsibility.\n\nIndependence.\n\nThe carefree university years slowly became memories.\n\nLife was moving forward.\n\nWhether they were ready or not.\n\nOne evening, nearly three years after graduation, Brian sat alone in his small office reviewing documents.\n\nThe business was beginning to stabilize.\n\nNot successful yet.\n\nBut moving in the right direction.\n\nHis phone vibrated.\n\nA message.\n\nHe glanced at the screen.\n\nThe sender's name made him pause.\n\nDiana.\n\nA smile appeared without him realizing it.\n\nThe message was simple.\n\nHi stranger. Are you still alive?\n\nBrian laughed quietly.\n\nThen replied.\n\nBarely.\n\nSeconds later another message arrived.\n\nGood. I was starting to think success had made you forget everyone.\n\nBrian leaned back in his chair.\n\nFor the first time in a long while, memories of university returned vividly.\n\nThe rehearsal hall.\n\nCultural Night.\n\nConversations beneath trees.\n\nRainy afternoons.\n\nA friendship that had somehow survived distance and time.\n\nNeither of them knew it yet.\n\nBut that simple message was about to change everything.\n\nBecause some connections fade away.\n\nOthers wait patiently for the right moment to begin again."
