      title: "Chapter 12 – A Promise of Forever",
      textAlign: "justify",
      subtitle: "The Beginning of Forever",
      text: "Brian did not sleep much that night.\n\nAfter Diana's call, he remained seated in his living room long after midnight.\n\nThe question her parents had asked lingered in his mind.\n\nIs there something going on between you two?\n\nFor months, both of them had avoided answering that question.\n\nNot because they did not know.\n\nBecause saying it aloud would change everything.\n\nUntil now, they had hidden behind friendship.\n\nBehind history.\n\nBehind distance.\n\nBut the truth was becoming impossible to ignore.\n\nSomewhere between the phone calls, the road trips and the countless conversations, something had changed.\n\nSomething important.\n\nAnd neither of them could pretend otherwise anymore.\n\nThe following week passed slowly.\n\nBrian buried himself in work.\n\nYet no number of meetings or deadlines could silence his thoughts.\n\nEvery road seemed to lead back to Diana.\n\nEvery plan seemed to include her.\n\nFor the first time in years, he found himself imagining a future that extended beyond business goals and financial success.\n\nA future shared with someone else.\n\nThe realization was both exciting and terrifying.\n\nOn Thursday evening, Diana called.\n\nHer voice sounded unusually quiet.\n\n\"Long day?\"\n\nBrian asked.\n\n\"A little.\"\n\nThere was a pause.\n\nThen another.\n\nBrian immediately noticed.\n\nSomething was different.\n\n\"Diana.\"\n\n\"Hmm?\"\n\n\"What's wrong?\"\n\n\"Nothing.\"\n\n\"You've never been good at lying.\"\n\nThat earned a laugh.\n\nA small one.\n\nBut a laugh nonetheless.\n\nFor a moment she remained silent.\n\nThen she spoke.\n\n\"My mother asked again.\"\n\nBrian smiled.\n\n\"About us?\"\n\n\"Yes.\"\n\n\"And what did you tell her?\"\n\nAnother pause.\n\nThe longest yet.\n\nFinally, Diana answered.\n\n\"I told her I wasn't sure.\"\n\nBrian stared out the window.\n\n\"I see.\"\n\n\"It wasn't because I don't know how I feel.\"\n\nThe words came softly.\n\nAlmost cautiously.\n\nBrian's heartbeat quickened.\n\n\"Then why?\"\n\n\"Because I didn't know how you felt.\"\n\nSilence.\n\nNot awkward silence.\n\nThe kind that arrives when two people stand at the edge of a life-changing conversation.\n\nBrian took a deep breath.\n\nThen spoke honestly.\n\n\"I think you already know.\"\n\nFor a moment neither said anything.\n\nThen he heard her laugh.\n\nNot because something was funny.\n\nBecause she was relieved.\n\n\"I was beginning to wonder if I'd have to say it first.\"\n\nBrian laughed too.\n\n\"You probably still will.\"\n\n\"Typical.\"\n\nThey both laughed.\n\nYet beneath the humour was something else.\n\nA certainty.\n\nFor the first time, neither was hiding.\n\nThe following weekend, Brian travelled to Nyeri again.\n\nThe journey felt different.\n\nNot because the road had changed.\n\nBecause he had.\n\nThe uncertainty that once accompanied every trip was gone.\n\nIn its place was clarity.\n\nWhen he arrived, Diana was waiting near the same café where they had first reunited.\n\nThe moment she saw him, she smiled.\n\nBrian smiled back.\n\nNeither rushed forward.\n\nNeither needed to.\n\nSomething had settled between them.\n\nSomething steady.\n\nSomething real.\n\nThey spent the afternoon walking through town.\n\nTalking.\n\nLaughing.\n\nSharing dreams they had never shared before.\n\nNot dreams about careers.\n\nOr business.\n\nOr achievements.\n\nDreams about life.\n\nAbout family.\n\nAbout the future.\n\nThe conversation felt natural.\n\nAs if it had been waiting years to happen.\n\nLater that evening, they found themselves sitting beneath a quiet sky on the outskirts of town.\n\nThe air was cool.\n\nThe stars bright.\n\nThe sounds of distant conversations drifted through the darkness.\n\nFor several minutes neither spoke.\n\nThen Brian turned toward her.\n\n\"Diana.\"\n\nShe looked at him.\n\nThe seriousness in his voice immediately captured her attention.\n\n\"I spent a long time thinking success was the most important thing in life.\"\n\nDiana listened quietly.\n\n\"I thought if I worked hard enough, built enough, achieved enough, everything else would eventually make sense.\"\n\n\"And now?\"\n\nBrian smiled.\n\n\"Now I think some things matter more.\"\n\nDiana's eyes never left his.\n\nThe silence between them deepened.\n\nNeither looked away.\n\nNeither needed to.\n\nFinally, Brian spoke.\n\nThe words he had carried in his heart for months.\n\nPerhaps years.\n\n\"I don't want to imagine my future without you in it.\"\n\nDiana's eyes filled with tears.\n\nNot tears of sadness.\n\nTears of certainty.\n\nThe kind that come when your heart finally hears what it has always hoped for.\n\nFor a moment she could not speak.\n\nThen she smiled.\n\nA beautiful, trembling smile.\n\n\"Good.\"\n\nBrian laughed softly.\n\n\"Good?\"\n\n\"Because I don't want to imagine mine without you either.\"\n\nThe words settled gently between them.\n\nSimple.\n\nHonest.\n\nEnough.\n\nAt that moment, neither needed grand speeches.\n\nNeither needed promises written on paper.\n\nTheir hearts had already chosen.\n\nMonths later, surrounded by family and friends, Brian formally asked for Diana's hand in marriage.\n\nThe answer surprised nobody.\n\nEspecially Diana.\n\nBecause in truth, that answer had begun forming years earlier.\n\nOn a university campus.\n\nIn conversations that seemed ordinary at the time.\n\nIn friendships that refused to fade.\n\nIn phone calls that arrived seven years later.\n\nAnd on a road that led from Nairobi to Nyeri.\n\nA road that ultimately led them to each other.\n\nAs celebrations began and plans for the future took shape, Brian found himself reflecting on the journey.\n\nThe years.\n\nThe distance.\n\nThe timing.\n\nThe countless moments that could have pulled them apart forever.\n\nYet somehow, they had found their way back.\n\nAnd now a new chapter awaited them.\n\nOne that neither would walk alone."
