      part: "PART THREE — FOUNDATIONS",
      endMessage: "< End of Chapter 13 – The White Wedding >",
      subtitle: "A Promise Bigger Than Two",
      text: "The morning of the wedding arrived with a strange kind of silence.\n\nDiana had imagined this day many times.\n\nSometimes she had imagined a grand ceremony.\n\nSometimes a small one.\n\nSometimes she had wondered whether it would ever happen at all.\n\nBut she had never imagined standing before a mirror in a white wedding gown with her daughter Amara sitting quietly on the bed behind her.\n\n\"Daddy Brian is coming today,\" Amara said.\n\nDiana smiled at her reflection.\n\n\"Yes, sweetheart.\"\n\nAmara swung her legs beneath the edge of the bed.\n\n\"Then he's going to be my daddy forever?\"\n\nDiana turned.\n\nShe looked at her daughter for several seconds.\n\nThen she walked over and knelt in front of her.\n\n\"You know Brian loves you.\"\n\nThe girl nodded.\n\n\"Yes.\"\n\n\"And today, he is becoming part of our family.\"\n\nAmara smiled.\n\n\"I already think he's family.\"\n\nDiana's eyes filled with tears.\n\nShe kissed her forehead.\n\n\"Then today is going to be a very special day.\"\n\nBrian had known about Diana's daughter , Amara from the beginning.\n\nHe had not been frightened by the responsibility.\n\nIf anything, he had been drawn closer to Diana because of the way she loved her child.\n\nShe was a young mother.\n\nStrong.\n\nProtective.\n\nIndependent.\n\nAnd there had always been a part of her story she rarely discussed.\n\nThe girl's biological father had never truly been present in her life.\n\nDiana had learned to raise Amara without depending on someone who had chosen not to stay.\n\nBrian never judged her for it.\n\nHe never asked questions that caused unnecessary pain.\n\nInstead, he simply showed up.\n\nAt first, he was just Brian.\n\nThen he became the man who brought her little gifts.\n\nThe man who listened to her school stories.\n\nThe man who remembered her favorite sweets.\n\nThe man she called whenever she wanted to tell someone something exciting.\n\nWithout realizing it, Brian had become something more.\n\nA father in everything except name.\n\nAt the church, Brian stood at the front.\n\nHis hands were steady.\n\nHis heart wasn't.\n\nThen the doors opened.\n\nDiana appeared.\n\nThe entire church seemed to disappear around her.\n\nBrian saw only her.\n\nAnd then he noticed Amara walking beside her.\n\nShe looked toward him.\n\nBrian smiled.\n\nShe smiled back.\n\nFor a moment, Brian's eyes filled with tears.\n\nThis wasn't only the woman he loved walking toward him.\n\nIt was the family he had chosen.\n\nThe ceremony was beautiful.\n\nThere were prayers.\n\nMusic.\n\nLaughter.\n\nTears.\n\nPromises.\n\nWhen Brian and Diana exchanged vows, they promised to stand together through whatever life brought them.\n\nBut when Brian looked at Amara  sitting in the front row, he made another promise silently.\n\nI will never make you feel like you are less than my own.\n\nHe didn't say it aloud.\n\nHe didn't need to.\n\nAfter the ceremony, Amara ran toward him.\n\n\"Daddy Brian!\"\n\nBrian bent down and opened his arms.\n\nShe jumped into them.\n\nHe laughed.\n\n\"Careful.\"\n\nShe held him tightly.\n\n\"You're my daddy now.\"\n\nBrian looked over her shoulder at Diana.\n\nDiana was crying.\n\nBrian smiled.\n\n\"Yes.\"\n\nHe hugged the Amara closer.\n\n\"Always.\"\n\nThat evening, after the guests had gone and the music had faded, Brian and Diana finally had a quiet moment together.\n\nAmara  was asleep in the room nearby.\n\nDiana sat beside him.\n\n\"We're really married.\"\n\nBrian smiled.\n\n\"We are.\"\n\nShe leaned against him.\n\n\"Are you happy?\"\n\nHe looked toward the bedroom.\n\nThen back at her.\n\n\"More than you know.\"\n\nDiana took his hand.\n\nBrian squeezed it.\n\nThere was something different about the future now.\n\nIt wasn't simply his future.\n\nIt wasn't simply hers.\n\nIt belonged to all three of them.\n\nAnd somewhere inside that realization, Brian understood that the wedding had not ended their story.\n\nIt had begun the most important part.",
