      text: "\nDiana didn't become suspicious overnight.\n\nIt happened slowly.\n\nA late arrival here.\n\nA secretive phone call there.\n\nA business trip.\n\nA second phone.\n\nA change in Brian's behavior.\n\nNone of it meant anything by itself.\n\nTogether, they became something she couldn't ignore.\n\nShe began watching him.\n\nNot intentionally.\n\nAt least, that's what she told herself.\n\nShe noticed when he turned his phone face down.\n\nShe noticed when he stepped outside to answer certain calls.\n\nShe noticed when he became uncomfortable whenever she asked about work.\n\nAnd she noticed something else.\n\nBrian was worried.\n\nHe was hiding something.\n\nBut she didn't know whether the secret was another woman or something far more dangerous.\n\nOne Saturday, Brian was helping Amara with her schoolwork.\n\nCassy was playing beside them.\n\nDiana watched from the kitchen.\n\n\"Daddy, is this answer correct?\"\n\nBrian leaned over the book.\n\n\"Almost.\"\n\nAmara frowned.\n\n\"What did I do wrong?\"\n\n\"You forgot this part.\"\n\nHe explained it patiently.\n\nAmara smiled.\n\n\"You're better than my teacher.\"\n\nBrian laughed.\n\n\"Don't let your teacher hear that.\"\n\nDiana smiled.\n\nFor a moment, everything felt normal.\n\nThen Brian's phone vibrated.\n\nHe looked at it.\n\nHis expression immediately changed.\n\nHe stood.\n\n\"I'll be outside.\"\n\nDiana watched him leave.\n\nAmara continued writing.\n\nBut Diana wasn't listening anymore.\n\nShe was listening to the faint sound of Brian's voice outside.\n\nLow.\n\nSerious.\n\nConcerned.\n\nAfter several minutes, he came back.\n\nDiana looked at him.\n\n\"Problem?\"\n\n\"No.\"\n\n\"Who was it?\"\n\n\"Business.\"\n\n\"Is everything okay?\"\n\n\"Yes.\"\n\nHe smiled.\n\nBut it didn't reach his eyes.\n\nLater that evening, Diana found a receipt in Brian's jacket.\n\nA restaurant.\n\nTwo meals.\n\nTwo drinks.\n\nShe stared at it.\n\nShe checked the date.\n\nIt was the same evening Brian had told her he had been working late.\n\nHer heart began beating faster.\n\nShe waited until he came home.\n\n\"What is this?\"\n\nBrian looked at the receipt.\n\n\"That's from a business dinner.\"\n\n\"With who?\"\n\n\"A client.\"\n\n\"Who?\"\n\nHe hesitated.\n\n\"A woman.\"\n\nDiana's stomach tightened.\n\n\"What woman?\"\n\n\"Her name is Vanessa.\"\n\nThere it was.\n\nA name.\n\nA real person.\n\nDiana tried to remain calm.\n\n\"Why didn't you tell me?\"\n\n\"Because it was business.\"\n\n\"Then why did you hide it?\"\n\n\"I didn't hide it.\"\n\n\"You never mentioned her.\"\n\nBrian sighed.\n\n\"Diana, not every woman I meet is someone I'm having an affair with.\"\n\nShe stared at him.\n\n\"I didn't say you were having an affair.\"\n\n\"You were thinking it.\"\n\nShe looked away.\n\n\"Maybe.\"\n\nBrian walked closer.\n\n\"There is nothing between me and Vanessa.\"\n\n\"Then what is between you?\"\n\n\"Business.\"\n\n\"What kind of business?\"\n\nBrian became quiet.\n\n\"Complicated business.\"\n\nDiana shook her head.\n\n\"Everything is complicated with you now.\"\n\nA few days later, Diana went to Brian's office unexpectedly.\n\nShe wanted to surprise him.\n\nInstead, she saw Vanessa.\n\nThe woman from the receipt.\n\nVanessa stood outside Brian's office holding a folder.\n\nShe looked at Diana.\n\nThen at Brian.\n\nBrian's face changed.\n\n\"Diana.\"\n\nShe smiled politely.\n\n\"I brought lunch.\"\n\nVanessa extended her hand.\n\n\"I'm Vanessa.\"\n\nDiana shook it.\n\n\"Diana.\"\n\nVanessa nodded.\n\n\"I've heard about you.\"\n\nDiana's heart skipped.\n\n\"You have?\"\n\nVanessa glanced at Brian.\n\n\"Yes.\"\n\nThere was something strange in the exchange.\n\nSomething Diana couldn't explain.\n\nVanessa turned to Brian.\n\n\"We'll continue tomorrow.\"\n\nThen she left.\n\nDiana watched her disappear.\n\n\"Who is she?\"\n\n\"I told you.\"\n\n\"Business?\"\n\n\"Yes.\"\n\nDiana nodded.\n\n\"Okay.\"\n\nBut she wasn't convinced.\n\nThat evening, Brian received another warning.\n\nThis time, the message was direct.\n\nThey know about the transfer.\n\nBrian stared at the screen.\n\nAnother message followed.\n\nIf you don't fix this, they will come after you personally.\n\nBrian's blood ran cold.\n\nHe deleted the messages.\n\nThen he sat alone in his office.\n\nThe business problem was no longer just a business problem.\n\nSomeone was using his company's financial records against him.\n\nSomeone knew about money he had moved.\n\nSomeone knew about the people he was dealing with.\n\nAnd someone was getting closer.\n\nBrian thought about Diana.\n\nAmara.\n\nCassy.\n\nHis jaw tightened.\n\nHe couldn't let anyone bring danger to his family.\n\nThat was why he kept silent.\n\nHe didn't know that his silence was beginning to create a different kind of danger inside his home.",
